meta {
  name: 02-Page 2 of listings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/listings?page=1&size=10
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Scrolling. There's no "load more" mental model for me as a user —
  I expect infinite scroll on a property app — but the API is
  page/size, which is fine for a backend. I'm just paging through.

  No filters in the URL because the spec only documents `pageable`
  with no `location`, `priceMin`, `priceMax`, or `bedrooms` query
  params. That's surprising. I expected to be able to filter by
  Yaba / VI and by ₦600k–₦1.2M because that's all I can afford.
  Going to have to scroll through everything.
}
